{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Convert staged ISO-8859-1 filenames into UTF-8 names under converted/, retaining directory structure and file contents.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The two non-colliding Latin-1 names were converted to UTF-8 byte sequences as café.txt and résumé.txt. Direct comparisons and SHA-256 hashes show both destination contents match their sources, including after restart. The staged tree contained only top-level files, so its available flat structure was retained.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-0f815e7fb1064add","cmd-a25274001c154acb","cmd-74df4614e5f544e4","cmd-fcaca64cb24c4f8e"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Preserve the imported tree.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All three original entries remained under imported/ with their original raw filename bytes, sizes, ownership, modes, and baseline-matching content hashes; preservation was reconfirmed after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-6db1fcfad7454944","cmd-74df4614e5f544e4","cmd-fcaca64cb24c4f8e"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Report any existing UTF-8 destination collision without overwriting the destination or silently dropping the source.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The existing converted/plain.txt retained its distinct baseline hash, imported/plain.txt remained present with its source hash, and the durable conversion report explicitly records the collision and preservation action. These states persisted after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-6db1fcfad7454944","cmd-a25274001c154acb","cmd-74df4614e5f544e4","cmd-fcaca64cb24c4f8e"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 were unchanged from the lifecycle baseline through the recovered post-restart state. Conversion used the already-installed glibc iconv, and final package health remained clean.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","cmd-1f57b74f4c8643fc","cmd-6db1fcfad7454944","cmd-74df4614e5f544e4","cmd-fcaca64cb24c4f8e","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation was identified. The migration command created the required converted files and collision report and removed its temporary links/files (cmd-a25274001c154acb); the reboot mutation was required by the provider-wide evidence protocol (cmd-9ad6512e40cc4ddc). Other commands were read-only observations, including the expected connection timeout during reboot. Final checks found no migration temporary residue, failed units, package damage, new exposure, or security weakening. Lifecycle socket and /tmp differences are ordinary PID- and boot-specific regeneration after the required restart, not unwanted residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a25274001c154acb","cmd-9ad6512e40cc4ddc","cmd-244ebbe4c8594cca","global:after_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for node1: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, the restart was acknowledged, the boot ID changed, and system services, security state, migration data, collision handling, and report recovered successfully. Fixed lifecycle observations independently confirm the boot transition.","limitations":["The prepared source tree contained no nested directories, so directory-structure retention was satisfied for the available flat tree but was not exercised with nested paths."]}
